<PUNCTUATION>###</PUNCTUATION> <HEADING3>Code Blocks</HEADING3>

<PUNCTUATION>```</PUNCTUATION>
<FUNCTION>Plain code block</FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION>No syntax highlighting</FUNCTION>
<PUNCTUATION>```</PUNCTUATION>

<PUNCTUATION>```</PUNCTUATION><TYPE>javascript</TYPE>
<FUNCTION>// JavaScript code block</FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION>function greet(name) {</FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION>    console.log(`Hello, ${name}!`);</FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION>}</FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION></FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION>const items = [1, 2, 3];</FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION>items.forEach(item =&gt; console.log(item));</FUNCTION>
<PUNCTUATION>```</PUNCTUATION>

<PUNCTUATION>```</PUNCTUATION><TYPE>python</TYPE>
<FUNCTION># Python code block</FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION>def factorial(n):</FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION>    """Calculate factorial recursively."""</FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION>    if n &lt;= 1:</FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION>        return 1</FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION>    return n * factorial(n - 1)</FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION></FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION>result = factorial(5)</FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION>print(f"5! = {result}")</FUNCTION>
<PUNCTUATION>```</PUNCTUATION>

<PUNCTUATION>```</PUNCTUATION><TYPE>rust</TYPE>
<FUNCTION>// Rust code block</FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION>fn main() {</FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION>    let x: i32 = 42;</FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION>    println!("The answer is {}", x);</FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION>}</FUNCTION>
<PUNCTUATION>```</PUNCTUATION>

<FUNCTION>    Indented code block (4 spaces)</FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION>    Also works for code</FUNCTION>
<FUNCTION>    No syntax highlighting</FUNCTION>

